From 9ad124c30e53b86f2ee2bbeab76abde1a69833cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: andesk <build@andesk.local>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:57:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] patches: build on a current Rust toolchain, and use the CN
 pub mirror
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two changes, both local to this machine's toolchain and network.

1. Cargo.toml — rust-sciter builds sciter's bit-flag values by transmuting into
   enums with no matching variant (e.g. SW_MAIN|SW_RESIZEABLE = 0x84, plus about
   23 more sites). Rust 1.78+ inserts a debug-only enum validity check on such a
   transmute and aborts with

     trying to construct an enum from an invalid value 0x84

   Upstream pins Rust 1.75 for the Sciter build; on a current toolchain the check
   has to be off for that crate. Release builds already default it off, so this
   affects dev builds only:

     [profile.dev.package.sciter-rs]
     debug-assertions = false

2. flutter/pubspec.lock — re-resolved against https://pub.flutter-io.cn instead
   of https://pub.dev, which is unreachable from here without a proxy. Also picks
   up a newer Dart/Flutter re-resolve (six transitive test packages added, version
   churn on about 10 others). No SDK constraint changed.

No other file in the tree differs from upstream.
---
 Cargo.toml           |   9 +
 flutter/pubspec.lock | 553 +++++++++++++++++++++++--------------------
 2 files changed, 308 insertions(+), 254 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index 1002586..0890a55 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -292,3 +292,12 @@ rpath = true
 
 [profile.dev]
 debug = 1
+
+# sciter-rs turns sciter's bit-flag values into enums with `transmute` (e.g.
+# SW_MAIN|SW_RESIZEABLE = 0x84, which has no declared variant). rustc inserts a
+# debug-only enum validity check on such transmutes and aborts:
+#   "trying to construct an enum from an invalid value 0x84"
+# Upstream pins Rust 1.75 for the Sciter build; on a current toolchain the check
+# has to be off for this crate. Release builds already default it off.
+[profile.dev.package.sciter-rs]
+debug-assertions = false
